  ImageLeft: {fileID: 0}
  Title: 'Mode Of Transmission:'
  Description: (Fluid beam) Human infection usually occurs when consuming contaminated
    foods and water, contact with infected faeces, as well as contact with infective
    animals, animal feed, or humans. Foods that pose a higher risk include meat, poultry,
    milk products, and egg products. In hospitals, the bacteria have been spread by
    personnel in pediatric wards, either on their hands or on inadequately disinfected
    scopes. Flies can infect foods which can also be a risk for transmission to humans.
  ImageRight: {fileID: 0}
